## What Problem This Solves

Fixes: strict browser SSRF policy cannot inspect redirect hops when navigation or a new tab uses an existing-session Chrome MCP profile.

## User Impact

When `browser.ssrfPolicy.dangerouslyAllowPrivateNetwork` is explicitly `false`, existing-session profiles now reject HTTP(S) navigation and tab opens before sending a Chrome MCP command. Use a profile with driver `openclaw` for strict navigation. `about:blank` remains available, and other policy modes retain their existing behavior.

## Why This Change Was Made

Reuse the browser navigation policy owner for a shared Chrome MCP preflight at both entry points. This applies the existing requirement for redirect inspection to a transport that cannot provide it. The added guard is needed at these two dispatch boundaries; no new configuration or state is introduced.

## Evidence

Validated head: `d3a9b11d11d21a6b51b7e4004c0e9a781f8452bd`.

The five focused browser suites passed 180 tests. Both added regressions failed against base production code and passed with this fix. Focused lint, formatting, extension-wide typecheck, and `git diff --check` passed.

```sh
pnpm test extensions/browser/src/browser/server-context.existing-session.test.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/server.agent-contract-core.test.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/agent.existing-session.test.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/agent.snapshot.local-managed.test.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/tabs.test.ts
```

## Real Behavior Proof

Executed the authenticated production browser bridge HTTP routes with a real isolated Chromium 148 session and the packaged `chrome-devtools-mcp` 1.12.0 subprocess on Linux/Node 24.20.0. No browser, MCP, DNS, HTTP, or policy adapter was mocked. A transparent stdio recorder forwarded the actual messages unchanged and counted only MCP tool names. Two local HTTP servers counted redirect and protected-destination requests.

The fixture's loopback host was explicitly listed in `allowedHostnames`, so destination checks allowed the controlled target while strict redirect inspection remained required. This prevents an unrelated private-address rejection from satisfying the test. The exact same redirect URL was then exercised with private-network permission explicitly enabled as the positive control.

| Scenario | HTTP result | Navigation/tab MCP dispatch | Redirect requests | Protected requests |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Strict `POST /navigate` | 400, redirect-inspection error | 0 | 0 | 0 |
| Strict `POST /tabs/open` | 400, redirect-inspection error | 0 | 0 | 0 |
| Strict `about:blank` tab | 200 | Real `new_page` call | 0 | 0 |
| Explicit non-strict navigation to the same redirect | 200 | Real `navigate_page` call | 1 | 2, including the page resource |
| Explicit non-strict tab to the same redirect | 200 | Real MCP tab creation | Not counted separately | Not counted separately |

The persisted profile and SSRF-policy configuration remained byte-for-byte unchanged. The diff changes no configuration reader, data schema, updater, migration, or profile format. Limits: this proves the production browser bridge, MCP subprocess and Chromium boundary in a source checkout; it does not claim a full Gateway/model flow or installed-package upgrade. Package-local SDK declaration resolution was unavailable; the extension-wide typecheck passed with zero errors.

Save the following harness outside the checkout as `/tmp/browser-real-mcp-proof.mts`, set `CHROME_BIN` to an available Chromium executable, and run from the clean checkout at the validated head:

```sh
CHROME_BIN=/path/to/chromium pnpm exec tsx --tsconfig tsconfig.json /tmp/browser-real-mcp-proof.mts
```

<details>
<summary>Complete real-browser reproduction harness</summary>

```ts
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import { spawn, execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';
import { createServer } from 'node:http';
import { mkdtempSync, readFileSync, writeFileSync, existsSync, mkdirSync } from 'node:fs';
import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';
import { join } from 'node:path';
import { randomBytes } from 'node:crypto';
import { setTimeout as delay } from 'node:timers/promises';

const repo = process.cwd();
const output = process.env.PROOF_OUTPUT ?? join(tmpdir(), 'browser-real-mcp-proof.json');
const root = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'browser-real-mcp-'));
process.env.OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR = join(root, 'state');
process.env.OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH = join(root, 'openclaw.json');
process.env.CHROME_DEVTOOLS_MCP_NO_UPDATE_CHECKS = '1';
const profileDir = join(root, 'chrome');
mkdirSync(profileDir);
const trace = join(root, 'mcp-tools.jsonl');
writeFileSync(trace, '');
const mcpEntry = join(repo, 'extensions/browser/node_modules/chrome-devtools-mcp/build/src/bin/chrome-devtools-mcp.js');
const recorder = join(root, 'record-mcp.cjs');
writeFileSync(recorder, `#!/usr/bin/env node
const {spawn}=require('node:child_process');
const {appendFileSync}=require('node:fs');
const child=spawn(process.execPath,[${JSON.stringify(mcpEntry)},...process.argv.slice(2)],{stdio:['pipe','pipe','inherit']});
let buffer='';process.stdin.on('data',chunk=>{buffer+=chunk;let i;while((i=buffer.indexOf('\\n'))!==-1){const line=buffer.slice(0,i);buffer=buffer.slice(i+1);try{const m=JSON.parse(line);if(m.method==='tools/call')appendFileSync(${JSON.stringify(trace)},JSON.stringify({tool:m.params.name})+'\\n');}catch{}}child.stdin.write(chunk);});
process.stdin.on('end',()=>child.stdin.end());child.stdout.pipe(process.stdout);
for(const s of ['SIGTERM','SIGINT'])process.on(s,()=>child.kill(s));
child.on('exit',(code)=>process.exit(code??1));
`, {mode:0o700});
let protectedHits = 0, redirectHits = 0;
const sink = createServer((_req,res)=>{protectedHits++;res.end('<title>protected-control</title>ok');});
const listen = (server:any) => new Promise<number>((resolve)=>server.listen(0,'127.0.0.1',()=>resolve(server.address().port)));
const sinkPort = await listen(sink);
const proxy = createServer((req,res)=>{
  if(req.url?.includes('/proof-redirect')) {redirectHits++;res.writeHead(302,{location:`http://127.0.0.1:${sinkPort}/protected`});res.end();}
  else {res.writeHead(200,{'content-type':'text/html'});res.end('<title>proxy-control</title>ok');}
});
const proxyPort=await listen(proxy);
assert(process.env.CHROME_BIN, 'Set CHROME_BIN to the local Chromium executable');
const chrome=spawn(process.env.CHROME_BIN,[
  '--headless=new','--no-sandbox','--disable-dev-shm-usage','--disable-background-networking',
  '--disable-component-update','--no-first-run','--no-default-browser-check',
  '--remote-debugging-port=0',`--user-data-dir=${profileDir}`,'about:blank',
],{stdio:'ignore'});
let bridge:any;
const summary:any={head:execFileSync('git',['-C',repo,'rev-parse','HEAD'],{encoding:'utf8'}).trim(),environment:'Linux, Node '+process.version+', Chromium 148, packaged chrome-devtools-mcp 1.12.0; real stdio transport and authenticated production browser bridge; isolated temporary state; exact fixture loopback host explicitly allowed by destination policy; strict redirect inspection remains required',root,scenarios:[]};
try {
  for(let i=0;i<100&&!existsSync(join(profileDir,'DevToolsActivePort'));i++)await delay(100);
  assert(existsSync(join(profileDir,'DevToolsActivePort')),'isolated Chrome started');
  const {resolveBrowserConfig}=await import(repo+'/extensions/browser/src/browser/config.ts');
  const {startBrowserBridgeServer,stopBrowserBridgeServer}=await import(repo+'/extensions/browser/src/browser/bridge-server.ts');
  const auth=randomBytes(24).toString('hex');
  const config={enabled:true,defaultProfile:'proof',ssrfPolicy:{dangerouslyAllowPrivateNetwork:false,allowedHostnames:['127.0.0.1']},profiles:{proof:{driver:'existing-session',userDataDir:profileDir,mcpCommand:recorder,color:'#112233'}}};
  writeFileSync(process.env.OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH!,JSON.stringify({browser:config}));
  const configBefore=readFileSync(process.env.OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH!,'utf8');
  const resolved=resolveBrowserConfig(config as any);
  bridge=await startBrowserBridgeServer({resolved,authToken:auth});
  const request=async(route:string,body:any)=>{
    console.log('real browser request',route);
    const r=await fetch(bridge.baseUrl+route,{signal:AbortSignal.timeout(90000),method:'POST',headers:{authorization:'Bearer '+auth,'content-type':'application/json'},body:JSON.stringify(body)});
    return {status:r.status,body:await r.json() as any};
  };
  const tools=()=>readFileSync(trace,'utf8').split('\n').filter(Boolean).map(line=>JSON.parse(line).tool);
  const blank=await request('/tabs/open',{url:'about:blank'});
  assert.equal(blank.status,200,JSON.stringify(blank));
  assert(tools().includes('new_page'));
  summary.scenarios.push({name:'strict about:blank real MCP control',status:blank.status,newPageCalls:tools().filter(t=>t==='new_page').length});
  const targetId=blank.body.targetId;
  const destination=`http://127.0.0.1:${proxyPort}/proof-redirect`;
  for(const route of ['/navigate','/tabs/open']) {
    const before={redirectHits,protectedHits,tools:tools().length};
    const result=await request(route,{url:destination,targetId});
    assert.equal(result.status,400,JSON.stringify(result));
    assert.match(result.body.error,/requires redirect-hop inspection/);
    assert.equal(redirectHits,before.redirectHits);
    assert.equal(protectedHits,before.protectedHits);
    const dispatched=tools().slice(before.tools);
    assert(!dispatched.includes('navigate_page')&&!dispatched.includes('new_page'));
    summary.scenarios.push({name:'strict '+route,status:result.status,expectedGuard:true,navigateOrNewPageCalls:0,redirectRequests:0,protectedRequests:0});
  }
  bridge.state.resolved.ssrfPolicy={dangerouslyAllowPrivateNetwork:true};
  const before={redirectHits,protectedHits,tools:tools().length};
  const permitted=await request('/navigate',{url:destination,targetId});
  assert.equal(permitted.status,200,JSON.stringify(permitted));
  assert(redirectHits>before.redirectHits&&protectedHits>before.protectedHits,'real redirect reaches controlled protected sink');
  assert(tools().slice(before.tools).includes('navigate_page'));
  summary.scenarios.push({name:'explicit non-strict real navigation control',status:permitted.status,navigateCalls:tools().slice(before.tools).filter(t=>t==='navigate_page').length,redirectRequests:redirectHits-before.redirectHits,protectedRequests:protectedHits-before.protectedHits});
  const opened=await request('/tabs/open',{url:destination});
  assert.equal(opened.status,200,JSON.stringify(opened));
  summary.scenarios.push({name:'explicit non-strict real tab control',status:opened.status});
  assert.equal(readFileSync(process.env.OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH!,'utf8'),configBefore);
  summary.persistedProfileAndPolicyUnchanged=true;
  await stopBrowserBridgeServer(bridge.server);bridge=undefined;
  summary.result='passed';
} catch(error) {summary.result='failed';summary.counters={redirectHits,protectedHits};summary.error=String(error);process.exitCode=1;}
finally {
  if(bridge){try {const m=await import(repo+'/extensions/browser/src/browser/bridge-server.ts');await m.stopBrowserBridgeServer(bridge.server);}catch{}}
  chrome.kill('SIGTERM');sink.closeAllConnections();proxy.closeAllConnections();
  await Promise.all([new Promise<void>(r=>sink.close(()=>r())),new Promise<void>(r=>proxy.close(()=>r()))]);
  writeFileSync(output,JSON.stringify(summary,null,2)+'\n',{mode:0o600});
  console.log(JSON.stringify(summary,null,2));
  process.exit(process.exitCode ?? 0);
}

```

